_image_url_https":"https:\\/\\/pbs.twimg.com\\/profile_images\\/1893219113717342208\\/Vgg2hEPa.jpg","name":"Grok","screen_name":"grok","highlighted_label":{"description":"xAI","badge":{"url":"https:\\/\\/pbs.twimg.com\\/profile_images\\/1769430779845611520\\/lIgjSJGU_bigger.jpg"},"url":{"urlType":"DeepLink","url":"https:\\/\\/twitter.com\\/xai"},"userLabelType":"BusinessLabel","userLabelDisplayType":"Badge"},"verified":false,"is_blue_verified":true,"verified_type":"Business"},"id":"muJPpDs58CY7EJ961PO7nuG7S","conversation_preview":[{"message":"Does alumium in a vaccine help your body?","sender":"USER","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]},{"message":"Aluminum is often used as an adjuvant in vaccines, which means it\'s added to enhance the immune response to the vaccine. Here\'s how it works:\\nEnhancing Immune Response: Aluminum salts help in attracting immune cells to the site of injection, thereby increasing the body\'s reaction to the vaccine antigen. This can lead to a stronger and longer-lasting immunity.\\nSafety: Numerous studies have confirmed that the amount of aluminum used in vaccines is safe. The body naturally contains aluminum, and the amounts in vaccines are small compared to dietary intake. The body efficiently eliminates aluminum, with most being excreted through the kidneys.\\nRegulation and Research: Regulatory bodies like the FDA in the United States, the European Medicines Agency (EMA), and the World Health Organization (WHO) have set guidelines for the use of aluminum in vaccines. These organizations continuously review the scientific literature to ensure the safety and effectiveness of vaccines.\\nConcerns and Misconceptions: There have been concerns about aluminum causing health issues like Alzheimer\'s disease or autism, but extensive research has not supported these claims. For instance, a large-scale study in Denmark found no link between aluminum in vaccines and autism. \\nSide Effects: Like any component of vaccines, aluminum might cause local reactions like redness or swelling at the injection site. These reactions are generally mild and temporary.\\nTo sum up, while aluminum in vaccines does help in creating a more robust immune response, which can be beneficial for vaccine efficacy, it\'s also a subject of public health debate due to safety concerns. However, the preponderance of scientific evidence supports its safety profile when used in recommended amounts in vaccines. If you\'re looking for more specific information or have concerns, consulting with healthcare providers or looking into peer-reviewed scientific literature can provide further clarity.","sender":"AGENT","grokMode":"NORMAL","mediaUrls":[]}],"destination":"destination_1","allowed_actions":["ASK_IT_YOURSELF"],"metadata":{"text":"Answer by Grok"}}}},"destination_objects":{"destination_1":{"type":"browser","data":{"url_data":{"url":"https:\\/\\/x.com\\/i\\/grok\\/share\\/muJPpDs58CY7EJ961PO7nuG7S","vanity":"Grok"}}}},"components":["details_1"]}', 'type': 'STRING'}}, {'key': 'card_url', 'value': {'scribe_key': 'card_url', 'string_value': 'https://t.co/cAKBoPQkl9', 'type': 'STRING'}}], 'card_platform': {'platform': {'audience': {'name': 'production'}, 'device': {'name': 'Swift', 'version': '12'}}}, 'name': 'unified_card', 'url': 'https://t.co/cAKBoPQkl9', 'user_refs_results': []}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1883906337903677584'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1737996846000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '2', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 27 15:54:06 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1883691494613340357', 'display_text_range': [14, 162], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [{'display_url': 'x.com/i/grok/share/m…', 'expanded_url': 'https://x.com/i/gr